  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training in the Conservation of Ancient and Historic Wooden Objects at the National Museum in Lagos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Museum in Lagos preserves one of the most important collections of Yoruba sculpture in the world. This project, which builds off the Museums pre-existing partnership with the Yale University Art Gallery, supports in-person workshops on the conservation of wooden objects for the Museums team of conservators.</narrative>
  </description>
